<title>HONG KONG: HK 97/98 budget surplus seen HK$31.7 bln - Tsang.</title>
<headline>HK 97/98 budget surplus seen HK$31.7 bln - Tsang.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong was expected to post an overall budget surplus of HK$31.7 billion for the 1997/98 fiscal year starting on April 1, Financial Secretary Donald Tsang said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>A year ago, Tsang forecast a surplus of HK$1.6 billion but revenues, boosted by the buoyant stock and property markets in particular, lifted the surplus to HK$15.1 billion.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6352</p>
